<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <RootNamespace>Rag.NET.Chunking.Templates</RootNamespace>
    <PackageId>Rag.NET.Chunking.Templates</PackageId>
    <Description>Domain-specific chunking templates for Rag.NET (Legal, Book, Academic Paper, Q&amp;A Pairs, Email, Resume)</Description>
    <VerifiedBy>integration</VerifiedBy>
    <VerifiedByReason>Three of the six templates now run over a real document through the real
      parser: the Academic Paper template over a real markdown paper
      (RealPaperExerciseTests), the Legal template over the Apache License 2.0 verbatim
      (RealContractExerciseTests), and the Book template over three verbatim chapters of a
      public-domain novel (RealBookExerciseTests). Those two new documents found #636 on
      first contact: Legal and Book returned a single chunk for any plain-text input,
      because the merger they delegate to classifies sections and never splits one, and the
      54 unit tests hand-build their section lists and so stood in for the parser rather
      than disagreeing with it. What stays unverified: the Q&amp;A Pairs, Email and Resume
      templates have no real document. A real Q&amp;A dataset was not available locally with
      its answers, and a real email thread or resume is personal data this project will not
      commit to a public repository.</VerifiedByReason>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <AssemblyAttribute Include="System.Runtime.CompilerServices.InternalsVisibleToAttribute">
      <_Parameter1>Rag.NET.Chunking.Templates.Tests</_Parameter1>
    </AssemblyAttribute>
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Rag.NET.Abstractions\Rag.NET.Abstractions.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Rag.NET.Chunking\Rag.NET.Chunking.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="CsvHelper" />
    <PackageReference Include="ClosedXML" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.AI.Abstractions" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.Abstractions" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
